{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Filer's note, owning the error: BOTH of my hypotheses on this ticket are refuted, and the investigator's two comments above have it right.\n\n1. First filing - Verified Gate concurrency group not keyed per-change. Refuted by me: the second cancellation hit the same 30-minute mark with no competing run created at that instant.\n2. Corrected filing - one global_support path selects ALL shards and busts timeout-minutes: 30. The SELECTION half is real and reproducible (change 1615 touches .github/workflows/test.yml, so select_shards returns all 7 shards), but it is NOT a defect: ac0f62be had already replaced the serial walking-skeleton gate with a per-shard parallel matrix giving each shard its own budget, and a real all-shards run passed with a worst shard of 20m22s. My two timeouts came from runs dispatched while main still carried the OLD serial workflow - reusable workflows resolve at main's ref, not at the patchset - so they were a rollout-window artifact that a rebase clears.\n\nThe trap in both cases was inferring a mechanism from run metadata without checking which version of the reusable workflow the run actually executed. The durable lesson for the next person: when a reusable-workflow job fails oddly, first read the 'Uses: ...@refs/heads/main (<sha>)' line in the job log and confirm that sha is the workflow you think you are debugging.\n\nChange 1615 is unblocked and rebased onto current origin/main (which also now carries 06335f71b1 'Skip mutation gate for pre-gate patchsets'); its patch set 3 already has LLM-Review +1. I am leaving the disposition of this ticket to the investigator and the coordinator - I am only correcting the misleading title I authored."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786513312918754001,"uuid":"b9466933-882e-4eb9-afb8-cb60e923af56"}